        "decoDesc": {
            "id": 5848064386323515636,
            "text": "Aggeloid remains would turn into a corrosive fluid when subject to abnormal levels of heat and pressure. In the process of Aggeloid formation, Ankhors would simply (and violently) \"mash\" the constituent inorganic materials of an Aggelos together to precipitate various reactions otherwise impossible in the real world. When Aggeloid remains are broken down, these unusual inorganic materials would undergo further changes. This is how the Precipitation Acid is made."
        },
        "desc": {
            "id": 3515343754439661251,
            "text": "Precipitation Acid is capable of dissolving various chemically resistant materials. It has plenty of uses in the AIC Factory."
